    "lore": "Italian East Africa wasn't the first conquest of the Italian Empire, but surely it is its proudest one. From the great heights of the Ethiopian mountains to the palm tree lined shores of Somalia, East Africa is home to endless fields of grain, unfathomable veins of gold and other minerals, loyal and hard-working natives, and just and honorable administrators. At least, that is the image constantly conveyed by Italian media and propaganda. In truth, East Africa is barely functioning despite the decent stewardship of its Viceroy, Amedeo di Savoia-Aosta. Rebels and partisans still haunt the territory's mountains and forests, and despite its vast riches, its economy struggles to develop in a mire of corruption. The crown jewel of the Italian Empire is starting to crack, and many believe that Italy will have to let go of its most precious conquest - either willingly or not..."
  },
